From c8c8c8775409a7ebff5b001fab47f10267a49e62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20P=C3=ADsa=C5=99?= <ppisar@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Feb 2025 12:29:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Port to ISO C23
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Building with GCC 15, which moved to ISO C23, failed:

    async_io.c: In function ‘aio_walk_slots’:
    async_io.c:233:8: error: too many arguments to function ‘fn’; expected 0, have 1
      233 |       (*fn)(slot);
	  |       ~^~~~ ~~~~

and also warned about:

    d3des.c: In function ‘deskey’:
    d3des.c:58:6: warning: old-style function definition [-Wold-style-definition]
       58 | void deskey(key, edf)   /* Thanks to James Gillogly & Phil Karn! */
	  |      ^~~~~~

This patch fixes it.

Signed-off-by: Petr Písař <ppisar@redhat.com>
---
 async_io.c |   2 +-
 async_io.h |   2 +-
 d3des.c    |  27 ++++--------
 region.c   | 126 ++++++++++++++++++++++-------------------------------
 4 files changed, 63 insertions(+), 94 deletions(-)

diff --git a/async_io.c b/async_io.c
index 7723d08..2c12682 100644
--- a/async_io.c
+++ b/async_io.c
@@ -221,7 +221,7 @@ int aio_listen(int port, AIO_FUNCPTR initfunc, AIO_FUNCPTR acceptfunc,
  * Returns number of matching slots.
  */
 
-int aio_walk_slots(AIO_FUNCPTR fn, int type)
+int aio_walk_slots(void (*fn)(AIO_SLOT *slot), int type)
 {
   AIO_SLOT *slot, *next_slot;
   int count = 0;
